## 9. FOOD ORDERING SYSTEM

This is one of the most important features of the website.

The customer must be able to select one or more meals, provide delivery or pickup details, review the order, and send the complete order to the restaurant through WhatsApp.

### Order form fields

When a customer clicks "Order Now", open an attractive, mobile-friendly order form.

Include:

1. Full name — required.
2. Phone number — required.
3. Selected food item or items — required.
4. Quantity for each item — required, minimum 1.
5. Delivery method — delivery or pickup.
6. Delivery location or address — required for delivery.
7. Area or neighbourhood — required for delivery.
8. Google Maps location link or location instructions — optional.
9. Preferred delivery or pickup date — optional.
10. Preferred time — optional.
11. Additional instructions — optional.
12. Payment preference — optional, such as cash on delivery, payment on pickup, or "Confirm with restaurant".
13. Order summary.
14. Food subtotal.
15. Delivery fee, if configured.
16. Total amount.

Use a clear note that delivery fees and availability may need confirmation by the restaurant.

Do not claim that payment has been completed simply because the customer selected a payment preference. Do not integrate a fake payment gateway.

### Order submission and WhatsApp redirection

After the customer completes the form and clicks "Place Order on WhatsApp":

1. Validate all required fields.
2. Confirm that the selected food items and quantities are valid.
3. Calculate the subtotal from current menu prices.
4. Calculate the total using the configured delivery fee, where applicable.
5. Generate a clear, readable order summary.
6. Save the order to Supabase if the database is available and the submission is valid.
7. Redirect the customer to WhatsApp using the restaurant's number.
8. Prefill a message containing all order details.
9. Allow the customer to press Send in WhatsApp to deliver the message to the restaurant.

Use this WhatsApp destination:

`https://wa.me/233571570126`

The international number must be digits only, without spaces, hyphens, or the leading zero.

Construct the WhatsApp message safely using `encodeURIComponent()`.

Example prefilled message:

"Hello Jales Kitchen! I would like to place an order.

ORDER DETAILS
Order reference: JK-XXXXXX

CUSTOMER DETAILS
Name: [Customer Name]
Phone: [Customer Phone]

ITEMS

1. Jales Special Jollof x 2 — GH₵90.00
2. Sobolo x 1 — GH₵10.00

Subtotal: GH₵100.00
Delivery fee: GH₵[Configured Fee]
Total: GH₵[Calculated Total]

Order type: Delivery
Location: [Customer Location]
Area: [Customer Area]
Preferred time: [Preferred Time]
Payment preference: [Selected Preference]
Additional instructions: [Instructions]

Please confirm availability and delivery arrangements. Thank you!"

The order reference must be generated dynamically.

Use `window.location.href` or a reliable new-tab approach to open the prefilled WhatsApp conversation. Ensure this works on mobile devices.

Important: WhatsApp prefilled messages do not automatically send messages. The customer must confirm and send the message in WhatsApp.

### Order reliability

If Supabase saving fails, do not silently claim that the order has been saved. Display a clear warning and provide a way to retry saving or continue to WhatsApp if the customer chooses.

Do not lose the order form data unnecessarily when an error occurs.

Prevent accidental duplicate submissions by disabling the submit button while processing.

Store timestamps in a consistent format and handle local display appropriately.

