## 11. SUPABASE DATABASE AND STORAGE

Use Supabase as the persistent backend.

Create a maintainable database schema with appropriate relationships, indexes, constraints, and Row Level Security (RLS).

Recommended tables:

### `profiles`

- `id` — UUID, references the authenticated Supabase user.
- `full_name` — text.
- `role` — text, restricted to authorized roles.
- `created_at` — timestamp.

Only authorized administrators should be able to assign or modify administrative roles. Never allow public registration to grant an administrator role.

### `categories`

- `id` — UUID.
- `name` — text.
- `slug` — text.
- `sort_order` — integer.
- `is_active` — boolean.
- `created_at` — timestamp.

### `menu_items`

- `id` — UUID.
- `name` — text.
- `slug` — text.
- `description` — text.
- `price` — numeric, non-negative.
- `image_url` — text, nullable.
- `category_id` — UUID, nullable foreign key.
- `is_available` — boolean.
- `is_featured` — boolean.
- `sort_order` — integer.
- `created_at` — timestamp.
- `updated_at` — timestamp.
- `deleted_at` — timestamp, nullable if implementing soft deletion.

### `orders`

- `id` — UUID.
- `order_number` — unique text reference.
- `customer_name` — text.
- `customer_phone` — text.
- `delivery_method` — text.
- `delivery_address` — text, nullable for pickup.
- `delivery_area` — text, nullable for pickup.
- `location_link` — text, nullable.
- `preferred_date` — date, nullable.
- `preferred_time` — text, nullable.
- `payment_preference` — text, nullable.
- `subtotal` — numeric.
- `delivery_fee` — numeric.
- `total` — numeric.
- `additional_instructions` — text, nullable.
- `status` — text with an allowed set of values.
- `created_at` — timestamp.

### `order_items`

- `id` — UUID.
- `order_id` — UUID, references `orders`.
- `menu_item_id` — UUID, nullable if an item is later deleted.
- `item_name` — text snapshot.
- `unit_price` — numeric snapshot.
- `quantity` — integer greater than zero.
- `line_total` — numeric.

Preserve item names and prices as snapshots so old order totals remain accurate after menu changes.

### `contact_messages`

- `id` — UUID.
- `full_name` — text.
- `phone` — text.
- `email` — text, nullable.
- `subject` — text.
- `message` — text.
- `is_read` — boolean.
- `created_at` — timestamp.

### `site_settings`

- `id` — UUID.
- `key` — unique text.
- `value` — JSONB or an appropriately typed field.
- `updated_at` — timestamp.
- `updated_by` — UUID referencing the administrator, where applicable.

Use appropriate additional tables only when they provide a clear benefit.

### Security requirements

Enable RLS on all relevant tables.

Public visitors may read only active, publicly visible menu categories and available menu items, plus the settings explicitly intended for public display.

Public visitors must not be allowed to list all customer orders, read contact messages, update order statuses, change menu items, or modify site settings.

Use Supabase Auth and verified administrator roles for privileged operations.

Do not rely on frontend checks alone for authorization.

If public customers need to submit orders without creating accounts, implement a carefully restricted submission mechanism. Validate the request server-side, restrict fields and allowed values, recalculate totals from trusted menu data, and apply rate limiting or equivalent abuse protection.

Do not expose privileged database credentials.

### Supabase Storage

Create a dedicated bucket for menu images, such as `menu-images`.

Configure appropriate upload permissions so only authorized administrators can upload, replace, or delete menu images.

Public access to images may be enabled if the images are intended to appear on the public website, but public write access must not be enabled.

Use stable public URLs or the appropriate Supabase image URL mechanism.

